Introduction

The  Compaq Evo T30 is a thin client.  One day, while shopping at  Weird Stuff, I happened to pick up several of these for a great price.  About half didn't boot, but I think this is because they don't have a plugin memory card.  My goal is to install Linux on them.";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}s:8:"relation";a:1:{s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:3:{i:0;N;s:7:"created";i:1205600787;s:8:"modified";i:1241050459;}s:7:"creator";s:9:"Rik Faith";s:11:"last_change";a:7:{s:4:"date";i:1241050459;s:2:"ip";s:10:"76.4.9.118";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:9:"linux:evo";s:4:"user";s:5:"faith";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";}s:11:"contributor";a:2:{i:0;N;s:5:"faith";s:9:"Rik Faith";}s:4:"user";s:0:"";}}